A '''Sailor''' (Japanese: '''ふなのり''' ''Sailor'') is a type of [[Pokémon Trainer]] that debuted in the [[Generation I]] {{pkmn|games}}. Originally they were often depicted as burly men in sailor suits flexing their muscles, though their actual physical shape varies between games. The sailor is one of two minor trainer classes, the other being {{tc|Guitarist}}, whose design features a visible tattoo. The [[Generation I]] sprites have an anchor tattoo and the {{Pokémon XD}} model has “FeeL GooD” tattooed across the knuckles reminiscent of "Hold Fast" tattoos. In {{game2|Diamond|Pearl|Platinum}} as well as in {{g|Brilliant Diamond and Shining Pearl}}, a sailor named [[Eldritch]] plays a minor part in the game's storyline.

They usually specialize in {{type|Water}} Pokémon, with the exception of using {{p|Raticate}} and the {{p|Machop}} evolutionary line.

In {{LGPE}}, Sailors battled outside of [[Gym]]s will award three {{i|Poké Ball}}s along with [[prize money]] upon being defeated.

