In ''[[EP019|Tentacool & Tentacruel]]'', {{Ash}} and {{an|Misty}}'s Pokémon rescued a Sailor.

In ''[[EP214|Mantine Overboard]]'', a Sailor gave Ash and {{Ashfr}} information about the ferry they missed.

In ''[[EP274|Hoenn Alone!]]'', a {{OBP|Captain|EP274|Sailor}} with the [[Animated series character recycling|exact same design]] helped {{Ash}} battle {{TRT}}. He was called a captain in the English [[dub]].

In ''[[AG124|Island Time]]'', a Sailor and a ship captain found Ash and {{ashfr}} after they escaped [[Wailmer Island]].

In ''[[BW125|Cilan and the Case of the Purrloin Witness!]]'', a Sailor helped the {{dec|Captain}} of the ship Ash and his friends were riding on investigate [[Mrs. Ripple]]'s lost jewel. He did this by interrogating [[Mr. Shaw]].

In ''[[SM027|A Glaring Rivalry!]]'', a Sailor had a {{pkmn|battle}} against {{an|Gladion}} and his {{DL|List of Pokémon with form differences|Lycanroc|Midnight Form}} {{TP|Gladion|Lycanroc}}, but they lost.

In ''[[JN047|Crowning the Chow Crusher!]]'', a Sailor was among the competitors in the [[Pokémon Grand Eating Contest]]. Though he managed to get past the first round, his {{p|Swalot}} was unable to continue due to {{TRT}} feeding it tampered cookies that filled up its stomach.

