==In the manga==
===Pokémon Adventures===
[[File:Eldritch Adventures.png|thumb|Sailor Eldritch and his family in [[Pokémon Adventures]]]]
====History====
====={{MangaArc|Red, Green & Blue}}=====
In ''[[PS010|Danger: High Voltorb]]'', a group of Sailors are the [[S.S. Anne]]'s guards. They are seen carrying boxes to the ship.

===={{MangaArc|Gold, Silver & Crystal}}====
{{main|Eldritch}}
Sailor [[Eldritch]] appears in this chapter, being one of the many sailors to work on the [[S.S. Aqua]]. In the {{MangaArc|Diamond & Pearl}}, he was revealed to have become a captain of the [[S.S. Sinnoh]].

====={{MangaArc|FireRed & LeafGreen}}=====
In ''[[PS270|Now You See Me...]]'', a Sailor was seen in command of the [[Seagallop|Seagallop Ferry]]. He would be seen frequently during the arc, transporting the [[Kanto]] [[Pokédex holder]]s from island to island.

====={{MangaArc|Emerald}}=====
In ''[[PS337|Epilogue]]'', multiple Sailors makes a cameo by appearing in the S.S. Sinnoh which is heading to the {{gdis|Battle Frontier|III}}.

====={{MangaArc|Omega Ruby & Alpha Sapphire}}=====
A Sailor was one of the people swarming the [[Mossdeep Space Center]] in ''[[PS606|Diancie Shines]]''.

====={{MangaArc|Diamond & Pearl}}=====
In ''[[PS365|Crafty Carnivine]]'' and ''[[PS366|Floatzel and Jetsam]]'', Sailors are seen in the [[Pastoria Gym]]. In the latter chapter, [[Crasher Wake]] orders the Sailors to dive in the water of Pastoria Gym to save {{adv|Platinum}} from drowning, but it turns out she left the water by herself without needing their help.

Multiple Sailors aboard the [[S.S. Sinnoh]] were shown to be taken out by a wild {{p|Gliscor}} in ''[[PS378|Grumpy Gliscor]]''. In ''[[PS382|Vexing Vespiquen & Unmanageable Mothim II]]'', those same Sailors witnessed the hatching of the [[Pokémon Egg]] found on [[Iron Island]] alongside Eldritch.

====={{MangaArc|Platinum}}=====
A Sailor briefly appeared in the {{gdis|Battle Frontier|IV}} in ''[[PS421|Clobbering Claydol]]'' as {{adv|Looker}} was searching for {{adv|Platinum}}.

